You do not need a browser to verify a token. A direct RPC call answers the same question the explorer does.

```typescript
import { getMint } from '@solana/spl-token';

const mintInfo = await getMint(connection, mintPublicKey);
const isMintRevoked = mintInfo.mintAuthority === null;
const isFreezeRevoked = mintInfo.freezeAuthority === null;
console.log({ isMintRevoked, isFreezeRevoked });
```

If both values are `null`, nobody can mint more supply and nobody can freeze your <Term id="token_account">token account</Term>. That does not make the token safe — teams find other ways to hurt holders — but it removes the two cheapest attacks.

The same session can pull supply and largest accounts with `getTokenSupply` and `getTokenLargestAccounts`, which is all you need to run the concentration check from the previous step without a third-party dashboard.
